    {
      "__comment": "Chamfer blade, north-west. Rotated 45deg so the square opening reads as an octagon that hugs the painted circle. Inner face lands on x+z=7, 6.36px from centre; the circle's radius is ~6, so it clears. Both outer tips finish inside the rim walls. Top sits 0.1px BELOW the y=14 rim: the blades have to overlap the walls (a diagonal seam cannot be tiled by axis-aligned boxes), so the tops are separated in depth rather than left coplanar and z-fighting. Recessed rather than proud so the seam reads as a masonry joint instead of catching light like a raised lip. 0.1px is 1/160 of a block -- a tenth of a texel -- but ~50x the depth precision at normal viewing range.",
      "from": [1, 10, 1],
      "to": [6, 13.9, 3.5],
      "rotation": {"origin": [3.5, 10, 3.5], "axis": "y", "angle": 45},
      "faces": {
        "up": {"texture": "#top"},
        "south": {"texture": "#side"}
      }
